.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt DESKTOP 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm desktop
.Nd Weston session, input and sound on the GNU system
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The GNU root starts Weston with kiosk-shell as the ordinary account
.Ql desktop ,
uid 1001, with a locked password.
The account belongs to the seat, video, render, kvm, input and audio groups.
Root can run a program as that account with
.Ql su -s /bin/bash desktop .
.Pp
.Xr init 8
supervises
.Pa /usr/libexec/rach2-desktop .
It makes
.Pa /tmp/.X11-unix
and
.Pa /tmp/.ICE-unix ,
mode 1777, where Xwayland listens.
It starts Debian's systemd-udevd, triggers existing devices, waits for
their events, then starts seatd as root with
.Ql SEATD_VTBOUND=0 .
The kernel has no virtual terminal interface.
The seat socket belongs to the seat group.
The user's session starts after the socket exists.
.Pp
The session has its own D-Bus bus and runtime directory,
.Pa /run/user/1001 ,
owned by desktop with mode 0700.
Weston uses headless with Pixman when no connector is connected.
A connected display uses DRM with Pixman, or GL when its card has a render
node; of several cards with a connected connector, the first by number of
those with a render node, then of the others, and Weston opens that card
alone.
.Sh DISPLAY
Weston runs the DRM backend as the card's master and holds the keyboard.
On QEMU's standard VGA, under
.Xr bochs 4 ,
it draws with Pixman on the output Virtual-1; on virtio-gpu, under
.Xr virtio-gpu 4 ,
with GL through Mesa's EGL on the render node, which is llvmpipe unless
the host gives virgl; on the firmware's framebuffer, under
.Xr fbdrm 4 ,
with Pixman on the output Unknown-1.
Weston's log in
.Pa /var/log/services
names the renderer and each output's modes, the current one marked.
udev gives
.Pa /dev/dri/cardN
the group video,
.Pa /dev/dri/renderDN
the group render and each
.Pa /dev/input/eventN
the group input, each mode 0660, as Debian's rules do.
.Pp
An output's resolution is set by a section of
.Pa /etc/xdg/weston/weston.ini
and a restart of the session:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[output]
name=Virtual-1
mode=1024x768
.Ed
.Pp
.Ql kill -HUP $(cat /run/rach2-desktop.pid)
ends the session and starts it again; Weston reads the file when it
starts.
.Pp
When Weston ends, by quitting or by a signal, SIGKILL among them, the
console takes the screen and the keyboard back and redraws its text, so
that the screen shows what it showed before Weston started, as
.Xr console 4
says.
The supervisor logs
.Dq rach2-desktop: session: ended; SIGHUP starts it again
and starts no session until SIGHUP.
.Pp
When the card the session draws on goes away, as when a virtual machine
that drew it through
.Xr vgpu-shm 4
dies or the GPU is given to a machine, the supervisor ends the session and
starts it again on the displays left, headless with GL on llvmpipe when
none is, and logs
.Dq rach2-desktop: session: its display BACKEND CARD RENDERER is gone; starting again .
Until the session draws on a card again, the next card with a connected
connector that appears starts it again there, with
.Dq rach2-desktop: session: display BACKEND CARD RENDERER appeared; starting again ,
which is how the session comes back to a GPU that Rach2's driver has
again.
A card that goes away and comes back under the same name and device before
the supervisor looks counts as gone.
A start on a card, whichever way it came, ends the wait for one: a card
that appears while the session draws on another, or headless since boot,
changes nothing; SIGHUP chooses the display anew.
Each start logs
.Dq rach2-desktop: session: started as PID on BACKEND CARD RENDERER .
udev's events for the cards, which
.Ql udevadm monitor
reads, wake the supervisor.
The device services go on; when one ends the supervisor exits and
.Xr init 8
starts it again.
.Pp
A program started from another session needs
.Ql XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/1001 ,
.Ql WAYLAND_DISPLAY=wayland-0
and
.Ql PULSE_SERVER=unix:/run/user/1001/pulse/native .
The compositor and sound server's output goes to
.Pa /var/log/services .
.Sh SOUND
PulseAudio runs
.Pa /etc/pulse/rach2.pa
alone, which loads module-oss over
.Pa /dev/dsp
without mmap as the sink oss_output and the source oss_input.
The module-suspend-on-idle module suspends each after five seconds
without a client that needs it.
When both suspend, PulseAudio closes
.Pa /dev/dsp ;
the next client resumes its endpoint.
Browsers use the user's native PulseAudio socket.
ALSA's default PCM converts formats with plug and opens its OSS plugin;
its control device is
.Pa /dev/mixer .
The kernel mixes both routes.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/xdg/weston/weston.ini
.It Pa /etc/xdg/weston/weston.ini
Compositor shell, Xwayland, idle and output settings.
.It Pa /run/rach2-desktop.pid
The supervisor's process id, which SIGHUP restarts the session by.
.It Pa /etc/pulse/rach2.pa
PulseAudio modules.
.It Pa /etc/asound.conf
ALSA's default PCM and control device.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pulseaudio 1 ,
.Xr weston 1 ,
.Xr bochs 4 ,
.Xr console 4 ,
.Xr drm 4 ,
.Xr fbdrm 4 ,
.Xr input 4 ,
.Xr virtio-gpu 4 ,
.Xr init 8
